        "id": 1012974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-23T22:32:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is confusing. You don\u0027t ever use the variables in a way that it makes sense to declare them outside the loop. If you\u0027re not going to do that (e.g. pass them to `AImageDecoder_setTargetSize`), you may as well declare them where they are used. (You actually never use `width`.)\n\nYou *could* assign them `AImageDecoderHeaderInfo_getWidth`/`Height`, and then randomize them and update them in the `AImageDecoder_setTargetSize` section, which would address my concern on line 131.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "ad846f699abb124307924eab752c832403669d17",
